 "note": "One assumption changed at a time from the Reference (the adopted settings), 2026\u20132050; bars are not additive and not a joint interval. The single-case carbon factors and the soil-order extremes (Raw / Organic) are bounds outside the Monte Carlo, not probability-weighted cases. Population rows: carbon is the floor area of the path times the Reference carbon per m\u00b2 of each year (an approximation, listed as a known issue in the CHANGELOG); the engine carbon of the population paths, carbon and boundaries together, is in data/aesa/results.json (population_paths) and is the one used in H11. Percentages are relative to carbon 2026\u20132050 (time-resolved accounting); fixed absolute terms such as soil carbon loss therefore show larger percentage effects than under whole-life accounting."
